# Cursor rules for Areeza

The full agent brain lives in CLAUDE.md — read it before coding.

Quick rules (see CLAUDE.md for the full version):
- Build Areeza: an AI legal filing platform for Uzbekistan. A workflow that completes a filing, NOT a chatbot.
- Ship the end-to-end loop (intake → classify → route → draft → validate → export) as vertical slices. Keep it runnable every hour.
- Stack: pnpm + Turborepo · Next.js 16 (App Router) · React 19 · TypeScript strict · Tailwind v4 · shadcn/ui · TipTap. Backend is Go (chi + gorilla/websocket) with Anthropic Go SDK behind `server/pkg/llm.Provider`. Postgres+pgvector provisioned (in-memory store today). On-device classifier in `services/classifier` (bge-m3 + LR tier-1 live; Qwen2.5-1.5B LoRA tier-2 trained). Local RAG in `services/rag`.
- Models: `claude-sonnet-4-6` for the interactive intake + validate, `claude-opus-4-8` for heavy document generation, `claude-haiku-4-5` for cheap extraction. All structured output via Go structs / JSON-schema-constrained calls — no hand-rolled JSON parsing.
- Legal STRUCTURE is data-driven (`server/internal/legal`); the model only fills content slots. Never let the model invent legal procedure.
- Generated documents must look like authentic Uzbek court documents — pull structure from `docs/legal-domain.md`. Real, not lorem.
- Never position as "AI lawyer" or give "legal advice." Language: navigation, preparation, validation, reduces rejection risk, human-in-the-loop.
- Workspace unit is a multi-issue `Situation` (`server/internal/situation`) — one conversation can produce many issues, parties, evidence, documents, advisories.
- Token discipline: most pipeline steps never call Claude (deterministic engine → cheap classifier → Claude only for the narrative draft + rare soft-pass). Context = structured facts, never the chat transcript.
- Deploy: Docker Compose on Coolify (web · api · classifier · rag · pgvector). See `docs/deploy.md`.
